# Once a window has been made, cancelling a command job runs its cancel
# handlers at once (otterPS's Invoke-OtterJobEvent on the window's
# dispatcher), not after the program's last line.
start command "ping -n 30 127.0.0.1" and call it before
on cancel of before
    say "cancelled before any window:" state of before
.
cancel before
say "after the first cancel"
create window into app
start command "ping -n 30 127.0.0.1" and call it sleeper
on cancel of sleeper
    say "cancelled:" state of sleeper
.
say "before cancel"
cancel sleeper
say "after cancel"
